sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila mauritiana Turing wavelength at 1.6 µm (Pass 1, free branch) — MorphoEval overall 78.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 judges the free (κ = 0) Schnakenberg branch at the assigned detail scale of 1.637 µm (log10 = -5.786), age 0 Ma. Analytical fastest-mode wavelength is 1.629 µm; the grid FFT peak is 1.562 µm. The pass-1 GIF is that spot field (official CV similarity 87.5 against the gallery ocellus). Side by side, spots are not the spiral illustration. The Dv/Du sweep is monotonic, and equal diffusion decays, but the animated endpoint does not yet show the assimilated ocellus. Weighted overall on rubric.yaml is 78.9. Overall 78.9/100 (faithfulness 75.6, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 66, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: datasets/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0/pass1_free_field.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 3018996 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 a1d10f117b81c3fd9c0c4c44e38ad96a71c98b5e6d11b9c919e5d1d856db1b09 (sha256 a1d10f117b81c3fd9c0c4c44e38ad96a71c98b5e6d11b9c919e5d1d856db1b09), spec_fingerprint bd0352c8a7daa2adc4a69dc6bf727442d96608f6e6279c8f820e0a58060ad4e4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: bd0352c8a7daa2adc4a69dc6bf727442d96608f6e6279c8f820e0a58060ad4e4; artifact_sha256: a1d10f117b81c3fd9c0c4c44e38ad96a71c98b5e6d11b9c919e5d1d856db1b09; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_mauritiana.jpg=0c64a140705a3c42..., datasets/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=837cc650677e6049...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: two morphogens can be stable at k = 0 and unstable at a finite wavenumber. | Murray 1981: that wavenumber is the intrinsic pre-pattern wavelength and it moves with the diffusivity ratio. | Glassford et al. 2015: the posterior lobe is a recent novelty in the melanogaster subgroup, elaborated in mauritiana.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a = 0.10, b = 0.90, D_v/D_u = 9.875, γ chosen so k_max sits on 1.637 µm. | Predecessor comparison uses the recorded kikkawai cellular wavelength 93.41 µm, not that slot's parameters.; transfer_boundary: The 1.637 µm target is this slot's assigned detail scale. Gompel 2005 and Glassford 2015 do not report that number.; does_not_claim: That the free spot field is a photograph of the genital arch. | That the gallery sepia spiral is a SEM.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=1.3]: Wavelength error is reported; Pearson, KS, and mask segmentation are not yet the scored endpoint.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.9]: Animated endpoint is the free spot field; the ocellus is only in the still comparison.",
            "remediation needed: Lock the growth GIF's final frames onto the assimilated ocellus (the nudged activator, not a paste of the photograph) and re-score CV similarity.",
            "remediation needed: Report specimen-versus-simulation segmentation (foreground fraction and structure-tensor coherency) with values that differ from the specimen reference.",
            "remediation needed: Score Pearson r, RMSE, and the KS statistic on the assimilated field in the measurement sidecar, and keep Pearson r above 0.98.",
            "remediation needed: Treat the equal-diffusion ablation and the monotonic D_v/D_u sweep as scored evidence on the pass-2 figure, not only as internal asserts." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.789"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

